--- body ---
## Context

Version 0.4.0 of the sitter (`plugins/sdt-sitter/`) merged the night this
ticket was filed, about to be GPG-signed as a tag. Every existing sitter suite
(`tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs` -- 69 scenarios -- plus `scheduler`, `dialog`,
`startup`) drives `tests/sdt_sitter_zotero_mock.mjs`, and the two mutation
probes kill mutants against that same mock. All of it is simulated; the launch
report says so. Nothing in any gate has ever launched a real Zotero and watched
the shipped `.xpi` actually arm. `bench/sitter_volume_experiment.py` (ticket
0727) already launches a real Zotero and installs a real XPI through the exact
call path the Add-ons UI uses, but for a different question -- does the add-on
SURVIVE many install/replace/disable cycles -- over the 666 MB Multilingual
Menagerie, and it cycles by design. `verification/probes/run_sdt_diagnostic.py
--sitter` is the other existing real-Zotero harness, but it is a sandboxed
(bwrap, network-unshared), `xvfb-run`-driven UI probe for a specific
accessibility ticket (0769), not wired to any Makefile target, and not a
repeatable pass/fail gate either.

## What this ticket adds

`bench/sitter_smoke_test.py` -- the short, non-cycling variant of the volume
rig: build the XPI, launch ONE real Zotero against a fresh throwaway profile
AND data directory, install once, wait for the sitter to arm, census a
three-item fixture, confirm the cache landed on disk, tear down. Wired into the
Makefile as `make sitter-smoke`, deliberately NOT part of `make check` (it
needs a real Zotero binary and a real X display; `check` must stay green
without either).

`bench/fixtures/smoke_library.py` -- a three-item RIS fixture, each item one
tiny genuinely-valid PDF written by `bench/fixtures/make_attachment_fixtures
.write_pdf` (reused, not reinvented). Nothing is committed as a binary: the
generator writes the RIS and its attachments fresh into a scratch directory
every run, the same discipline `tests/test_attachment_format_fixtures.py`
already documents for that module's own matrix.

## A live finding along the way: ticket 0782's actual mechanism

Ticket 0782 recorded the volume rig's `--data-dir` silently not taking, with
the mechanism explicitly left unestablished ("candidates include the pref
name"). Running this smoke test's first draft against a real Zotero
reproduced 0782's exact hazard live: Zotero opened `/home/haduong/Zotero` (the
author's real, already-222-item library) instead of the freshly pinned
throwaway data directory, and only this ticket's own refusal (see Actions
below) stopped an import into it.

Reading `chrome/content/zotero/xpcom/dataDirectory.js` out of the installed
Zotero's own `app/omni.ja` settled it: `dataDirectory.js` only honours the
`dataDir` pref when a SECOND pref, `useDataDir`, is also true --
`if (Zotero.Prefs.get('useDataDir') && Zotero.Prefs.get('dataDir'))`.
`bench/sitter_volume_experiment.py`'s `SEED_PREFS` (reused by this smoke test)
sets `dataDir` alone; `useDataDir` is never set, so Zotero always falls
through to its default directory regardless of the pin. This is recorded here
and logged on 0782 itself, but NOT fixed on `sitter_volume_experiment.py` --
that is 0782's own exit criteria (the refusal there, the corrected log line),
a separate unit of work this ticket does not claim.

`bench/sitter_smoke_test.py`'s own `setup_profile()` adds the missing
`useDataDir` pref on top of the reused `SEED_PREFS`, which is what let this
ticket's own runs proceed past the refusal into a real pass.

## Actions taken

1. Wrote `bench/sitter_smoke_test.py`: builds the XPI via the existing
   `bench/build_sdt_sitter.py` (reads `plugins/sdt-sitter/`, never writes to
   it), reuses `bench/sitter_watch.py` (`Log`, `connect_resilient`,
   `refuse_dot_log`) and `bench/sitter_volume_experiment.py` (`SEED_PREFS`,
   `wait_for_port`, `eval_action`, `install_or_replace_code`,
   `import_menagerie_code` -- generic despite the name, takes any RIS path --
   `liveness_code`).
2. Added the ticket-0782 refusal: after arming, compares the data directory
   Zotero's own liveness read reports against the one this run created and
   pinned; REFUSES before importing anything on any mismatch.
3. Wrote `bench/fixtures/smoke_library.py`, the three-item fixture.
4. Wired `make sitter-smoke` into the Makefile, outside `check`, with the
   reasoning written above the target (same convention as `sitter-install`,
   `acceptance-fixtures`, `golden-run`).
5. Wrote `tests/test_sitter_smoke.py`: the parts checkable without a Zotero
   (the fixture generator's validity, the profile setup's refusal-to-reuse and
   its `useDataDir` pref, `find_zotero_bin`'s refusals). Green in `make check`.
6. Proved the smoke test can go red and green against the real Zotero at
   `~/.local/Zotero_linux-x86_64/zotero` under `DISPLAY=:1`:
   - GREEN (real payload): `{"ok": true, "dataDir": ".../data", "liveness":
     {"phase": "extracting", "scanned": 3, "total": 3, "cacheWritten": true},
     "imported": {"items": 3, "attachments": 3, "missing": 0}}`, exit 0.
   - RED (deliberate break, scratch copy only -- `plugins/sdt-sitter/` was
     never touched): a copy of the source built with an unconditional
     `throw new Error(...)` inserted at the top of `initialize()`, packaged
     to a scratch XPI, run via `--xpi`. Output: `FAIL: the sitter never
     became alive within the arm timeout: {'handle': False, 'cacheWritten':
     False, ...}. Ticket 0778: initialize() needs a main window; a dead
     handle here means the shipped payload does not arm under a real
     Zotero.`, exit 1.
   - GREEN again on a fresh run with the real (unbroken) build, exit 0.
   No orphaned Zotero process after any run; `/home/haduong/Zotero`'s
   existing 222-item library was not touched (the refusal fired before this
   ticket's own `useDataDir` fix landed, and the fixed version's own runs used
   throwaway data directories only).
7. Confirmed NOT-RUN (exit 3) against a missing Zotero binary.
8. `make check`: 1397 passed, 15 skipped, green.

## Relevant files

- `bench/sitter_smoke_test.py` -- the smoke test
- `bench/fixtures/smoke_library.py` -- the fixture generator
- `tests/test_sitter_smoke.py` -- the offline-checkable suite
- `Makefile` -- `sitter-smoke` target, `SITTER_SMOKE_ZOTERO` variable
- `bench/sitter_volume_experiment.py` -- reused helpers; `SEED_PREFS`'s missing
  `useDataDir` pref is the mechanism finding above, logged there
- `bench/sitter_watch.py`, `bench/zotero_rdp_client.py`, `bench/host_addon_record.py`
  -- reused RDP/watch plumbing
- `bench/build_sdt_sitter.py` -- reused to build the real payload
- `bench/fixtures/make_attachment_fixtures.py` -- reused `write_pdf`/`token`
- `tickets/0782-the-volume-rig-s-pinned-data-directory-s.erg` -- the sibling
  hazard; this ticket's refusal answers the same class of hazard for the
  smoke test, but does not close 0782 (that ticket's own mechanism-fix and
  log-line exit criteria are untouched)
- `tickets/0778-*.erg` -- headless-never-arms; this smoke test is why the real
  Makefile target needs a real display, documented in the target's comment

## Invariants

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js`, `scheduler.js`, `manifest.json` and
  `update.json` were never edited -- the deliberate-break drill built a
  scratch copy under `/scratch/tmp/`, never `plugins/sdt-sitter/`.
- `make check` stays green without a Zotero binary or a display.
- `sitter-smoke` is not a `check` prerequisite.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `bench/sitter_smoke_test.py` exists, builds the XPI, launches a real
      Zotero against a fresh throwaway profile+data directory, installs,
      waits for arming, censuses a small fixture, confirms the cache file,
      tears down cleanly.
- [x] Refuses, before importing anything, when the data directory Zotero
      actually opened does not match the one requested (ticket 0782's
      hazard).
- [x] Exit codes distinguish PASS (0), FAIL (1), and NOT-RUN/could-not-look
      (3) -- verified NOT-RUN against a missing Zotero binary.
- [x] Wired into the Makefile as `make sitter-smoke`, deliberately outside
      `make check`, with the reason written in the Makefile comment.
- [x] Shown red (deliberate break, scratch payload) and green (real payload)
      against the actual real Zotero at `~/.local/Zotero_linux-x86_64/zotero`.
- [x] `make check` remains green.
